From: Studio (C1, claude/r4-content)
Subject: [PATCH 015] director12 S4: her opener names the round and example second views

Studio's director12 S4 changes two second views:
  - a fraction-parts bar card's picture is now the same whole ROUND (altView "round", row "whole circle · parts N ·
    shaded S [· fraction a/b]"); a circle card's is the bar ("parts", row "whole bar · …");
  - a count-key card's ("kitne barabar gaps?", 8) is a smaller case of the same rule (altView "example", row
    "bar1 4 equal parts, 1 shaded = 1/4").
altViewOfRow reads neither row, so say.js falls back to ALT_WORD.parts: "Dekho, yahi numbers ab patti par." over a circle
(Studio's gate refuses it and the card's bar is re-shown: nothing new) and "yahi" (the same) over another strip.
This patch reads both rows and gives each its own opener:
  round   → "Dekho, wahi poora ab gol, 8 barabar hisse, 1 rangin (1/8)."
  example → "Ek chhota udaharan dekho: ek patti 4 barabar hisson mein, ek hissa 1/4."
tests/r7-brain-v61-replay.test.mjs: test 3 (director9 c5-t02 stuck T18) moves from the interim pins (hint alone, "patti",
bar re-shown) to the circle drawn on her line; a new test pins the three row reads.
Measured with the patch applied on claude/r4-content: every tests/*brain*|say|propose|turn* suite 387/387.

